00:03:17.415 --> 00:03:23.095
>> I should have that by now. I'm just going to go over a couple things that are pertinent to the Board of Finance.

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:28.650
The assessor's office, the Board of Selectmen made a decision at their last meeting

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.770
to purchase an additional server license

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:36.330
and use a local copy of that as opposed to a cloud based service.

00:03:37.415 --> 00:03:39.495
That cost has increased.

00:03:39.895 --> 00:03:42.615
It'll basically be a $5,700

00:03:42.615 --> 00:03:45.015
bill to buy the server license,

00:03:45.575 --> 00:03:47.975
but that's a kind of a Microsoft,

00:03:48.375 --> 00:03:50.135
I don't want to say stupidity,

00:03:50.135 --> 00:03:50.775
but racket.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:56.140
Because they price them by the number of cores of the server.

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:01.820
So because we have a 16 core server, it's considerably more expensive

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.140
and they only sell them in two packs.

00:04:04.575 --> 00:04:12.735
So you can't get an individual license. But the good news is there have been a few other things where we would have probably installed

00:04:13.215 --> 00:04:17.375
an extra quote unquote server on the server if we had the ability.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:18.760
So,

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:30.280
you know, it is what it is. The intention from the Board of Selectmen is to take that money from the Reval Fund because it's for the assessor's office.

00:04:30.785 --> 00:04:36.225
And that basically what it is, is it allows them to continue using Vision appraisal.

00:04:37.185 --> 00:04:41.265
Vision allowed us to use their cloud based version

00:04:41.505 --> 00:04:44.305
while we were going through the appraisal process

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:49.630
because it's faster and easier for them to make changes when they control the location

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:51.870
of the software and the data.

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:55.150
But now that that's up, they either want us to pay,

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:57.710
you know, dollars 2,500, dollars 2,700

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:59.950
a year or install it locally.

00:05:00.485 --> 00:05:06.085
So, you know, it's basically a, you know, a two year payoff to install it locally,

00:05:06.245 --> 00:05:10.485
and it gives us one additional server license for future expansion.

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:13.525
We're

00:05:13.525 --> 00:05:22.380
getting ready to get in a really busy point for issuing transfer station stickers, so I would imagine that we're going to probably issue $10,000

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:23.420
or $12,000

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:26.380
worth of transfer station stickers in the next month.

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:29.500
So that's going to be ongoing.

00:05:30.635 --> 00:05:34.715
I also sent a notice to all boards, commissions and employees

00:05:34.875 --> 00:05:41.435
that they have until June 3 to make any significant purchases that they need out of their budget.

00:05:42.235 --> 00:05:42.955
And if not,

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:47.760
if they think they're not going to be able to do that by that timeframe,

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.480
then they need to let me know so that we can hopefully get the bills back

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:54.000
sooner

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:59.200
and not carry that on as far as we did last year, because that was kind of annoying.

00:05:59.645 --> 00:06:03.405
We were still chasing down stuff in September of last year.

00:06:04.205 --> 00:06:05.725
Building department,

00:06:08.525 --> 00:06:10.845
point and pay is up and running.

00:06:11.325 --> 00:06:13.805
