money back to the town. So

00:10:21.495 --> 00:10:23.975
not a ton, but it's better than nothing.

00:10:25.175 --> 00:10:30.375
We also put ourselves on both the state bid list and also the croc bid list.

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:36.510
State bid list for untreated salt or CRUD bid list for treated salt.

00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:39.390
So we don't know what the bids are,

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:44.830
but basically what happens is everybody who wants to be part of the bid process

00:10:45.095 --> 00:10:52.135
has to agree and sign ahead of time that they want to be part in that so they know how much they're contracting.

00:10:52.775 --> 00:10:59.335
And it's these are variable bids, you have to give them a minimum number of tons you're going to use.

00:10:59.870 --> 00:11:03.550
And then you can usually order two to three times that

00:11:04.190 --> 00:11:14.430
up to two to three times that. So we're doing the same thing that we did last year to save money. We're allowing ourselves to buy both treated salt and untreated salt.

00:11:14.835 --> 00:11:20.275
So we'll use the untreated stuff earlier in the year when it's warmer and save the treated salt

00:11:20.435 --> 00:11:22.035
for when it's colder.

00:11:22.995 --> 00:11:25.635
You know, and we've got more icing conditions.

00:11:26.115 --> 00:11:27.715
>> It's just a lower

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:31.940
freezing temperature salt just as got added as to lower the temperature?

00:11:32.260 --> 00:11:34.980
>> Yeah, basically what it is is it's,

00:11:35.140 --> 00:11:36.980
you know, most of it is

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:38.980
sodium chloride,

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:44.715
that's regular rock salt, and then they add magnesium chloride to it, which has a much lower,

00:11:46.955 --> 00:11:53.115
>> bigger freezing point depression. Yeah, so it's a mix, okay. Magnesium chloride, okay. Yeah,

00:11:53.275 --> 00:11:55.035
>> Bunker Hill Bridge,

00:11:55.515 --> 00:11:58.715
that's still slated for spring of twenty twenty four,

00:11:59.600 --> 00:12:06.720
which is good because even with this budget, we're not going have enough money to pay for it. So, it would be this budget plus some of that last

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:07.120
budget.

